  <text>
    <status value="generated"/><div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p class="res-header-id"><b>Generated Narrative: ConceptMap NgHivDiagnosisToICD11</b></p><a name="NgHivDiagnosisToICD11"> </a><a name="hcNgHivDiagnosisToICD11"> </a><p>Mapping from <a href="ValueSet-ng-hiv-diagnosis-concepts-vs.html">Nigeria HIV Diagnosis Concepts</a> to <a href="ValueSet-ng-hiv-diagnosis-icd11-concepts-vs.html">Nigeria HIV ICD-11 Diagnosis Concepts</a></p><br/><p>Mapping from <a href="CodeSystem-ng-hiv-diagnosis-cs.html">Nigeria HIV Diagnosis Codes</a> to <a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/6.2.0/CodeSystem-ICD11MMS.html">International Classification of Diseases, 11th Revision Mortality and Morbidity Statistics (MMS)</a></p><table class="grid"><tr><td><b>Source Code</b></td><td><b>Relationship</b></td><td><b>Target Code</b></td><td><b>Comment</b></td></tr><tr><td>cryptococcal-meningitis</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R4/codesystem-concept-map-equivalence.html#concept-map-equivalence-wider" title="wider">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>1F27.1 (Cerebral cryptococcosis)</td><td>ICD-11 1F27.1 Cerebral cryptococcosis is broader than the local diagnosis Cryptococcal meningitis. The more specific 1F27.10 asserts Cryptococcus neoformans and should only be used when that organism is established.</td></tr><tr><td>histoplasmosis</td><td><a href="http://hl7.org/fhir/R4/codesystem-concept-map-equivalence.html#concept-map-equivalence-equivalent" title="equivalent">is equivalent to</a></td><td>1F2A (Histoplasmosis)</td><td/></tr></table></div>
